WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.967
HIPAA training. Module 2. PHI, ePHI and identifiers.

2
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:12.967
PHI is health information that identifies a person, in any form.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.733
Three parts come together.

4
00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:18.233
It is about a person.

5
00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:22.200
It is about their health, their care, or payment for it.

6
00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:24.633
And it identifies them.

7
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:30.233
There are eighteen identifiers, and a name is only one of them.

8
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:37.500
HIPAA has two ways to de-identify information, Safe Harbor and Expert Determination.

9
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.033
Taking the name out is not one.

10
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.100
A saved screenshot.

11
00:00:43.433 --> 00:00:46.267
A file name with a patient's name.

12
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.100
An email subject line or calendar invite.

13
00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:53.433
A sticky note or printed schedule.

14
00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:00.100
Taking the name out and sending it on as safe is not de-identifying.

15
00:01:00.433 --> 00:01:06.200
De-identifying is the client's decision and process, so ask your lead.

16
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:07.967
Stop.

17
00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:09.367
Do not share.

18
00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:10.900
Ask your lead.

19
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.033
Now read the module.
